DTSTART:20270207T063000
DTEND:20270207T082000
SUMMARY:[RW] Long run (110 min)
DESCRIPTION:5 min warm-up\; 78 min easy\; 22 min steady finish\; 5 min coo
 l-down. Easy means RPE 2-3: you can talk in full sentences. Use your watc
 h's easy heart-rate zone if you have one. The last part is steady (RPE 4-
 5): finish tired\, not empty.\n\nWeek 11 (PEAK). Not medical advice\; pai
 n that changes how you move means stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-02-08-str1-strength-lower-body-@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20270208T183000
DTEND:20270208T185500
SUMMARY:[RW] Strength: lower-body strength (single-leg strength) (light) (
 25 min)
DESCRIPTION:Runner\, 5 km to half marathon: better running economy and rac
 e pace. Lift with 2-3 reps in reserve\, stop a set if form breaks. Streng
 th starts at least 3 hours after cardio (practice).\n\nWeek 12 (TAPER). N
 ot medical advice\; pain that changes how you move means stop.\nrampwise-
 plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-02-09-run1-sharpener-4-x-2-min@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20270209T063000
DTEND:20270209T070500
SUMMARY:[RW] Sharpener (4 x 2 min) (35 min)
DESCRIPTION:10 min warm-up\; 4 x (2 min threshold + 2 min easy)\; 8 min co
 ol-down. Short and crisp\, then stop. The taper keeps a little intensity 
 while volume drops (Bosquet 2007).\n\nWeek 12 (TAPER). Not medical advice
 \; pain that changes how you move means stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-02-10-bike_x-easy-ride-cross-trai@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20270210T063000
DTEND:20270210T071500
SUMMARY:[RW] Easy ride (cross-training) (45 min)
DESCRIPTION:8 min warm-up\; 32 min easy\; 5 min cool-down. Low-impact aero
 bic work next to the running: Mostly steady endurance (RPE 2-3\, 56-75 % 
 of FTP if you use power). Eat and drink on rides over 90 minutes.\n\nWeek
  12 (TAPER). Not medical advice\; pain that changes how you move means st
 op.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
